# Frontend Rules

- Keep frontend code in React/Vite TypeScript patterns (`pages`, `components`, `services`, `hooks`, `features`, `design-system`).
- Frontend services call backend APIs; do not implement backend/server runtime logic here.
- Respect strict lint quality: zero warnings is required.
- Prefer reusable components and shared UI primitives over one-off duplicated UI code.
- Keep naming consistent with existing codebase conventions and imports.
- Avoid introducing backend-only dependencies or server startup code in frontend.
